[OVERVIEW]
Windows Deployment Suite v2.3 is an all-in-one, standalone administrative 
utility designed for Windows image servicing, package management, and native 
solid archiving. 

It requires NO INSTALLATION. Run the executable as Administrator.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. FIRST LAUNCH & PERMISSIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Place the executable in a working directory (e.g., Desktop or external USB drive).
2. Right-click the application and select "Run as administrator".
   - If launched normally, the app will automatically request UAC elevation.
3. The dark theme and neon green accent will load by default. 
   - Use the right-hand COLOR swatches to change the neon highlight.
   - Use the DARK/LIGHT toggle switch to swap between dark and light modes.
   - Your preferences are saved automatically in theme.cfg and mode.cfg.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. TAB 1: WINDOWS DEPLOYMENT HUB
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This tab handles driver integration, image servicing, unattended automation, 
and workspace resets.

A. DRIVER BACKUP & RESTORATION:
   - "Backup Drivers":
     Exports all 3rd-party installed hardware drivers on the active PC into
     an "ExportedDrivers" folder located in your current app directory.
   - "Restore (Default)":
     Installs all drivers found inside the local "ExportedDrivers" folder.
   - "Restore (Browse...)":
     Opens a folder browser to select any custom driver folder on your PC or
     flash drive and installs every .inf file found inside it.

B. IMAGE SERVICING & SLIPSTREAMING:
   - "Scan & Slipstream Image":
     Automatically looks for an "install.wim" or "install.esd" in your working
     folder. If found, it lists all OS editions, prompts you for an Index number,
     mounts the image, injects all drivers from "ExportedDrivers", and unmounts
     with changes saved.
   - "Browse Image & Slipstream":
     Allows you to manually pick any .wim or .esd file from any drive and runs
     the same automated injection pipeline.

C. IMAGE INSPECTION & TRIMMING:
   - "List WIM Editions / Indexes":
     Prompts for an image and prints every Edition (Home, Pro, etc.) along with
     its Index number into the bottom console.
   - "Delete Unwanted WIM Index":
     Prompts you to enter an Index number to permanently delete from a WIM,
     shrinking the file size and leaving only the edition you want.

D. COMPRESSION & UNATTENDED SETUP:
   - "Compress Folder (Zip/WinRAR/WinZip)":
     Select any folder to compress using native Windows zip, WinRAR, or WinZip.
   - "Convert WIM to Solid ESD":
     Converts a standard install.wim into a heavily compressed install.esd
     recovery image (/Compress:recovery) for smaller ISO/USB sizes.
   - "Generate autounattend.xml":
     Instantly drops a pre-configured unattended XML answer file on your Desktop.
     This file automatically creates a local admin account ("User") and bypasses
     Windows 11 hardware restrictions (TPM 2.0, Secure Boot, RAM, CPU, Storage).
   - "Force DISM Cleanup / Reset":
     Use this if a mount operation gets interrupted. It unmounts stuck images,
     cleans stale mountpoints, and flushes temporary staging folders.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. TAB 2: APPXPULSE (BLOATWARE & PACKAGE MANAGER)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This tab audits and strips modern AppX/MSIX bloatware from your system.

1. Click "Scan Installed AppX Packages" to list user-level store apps, OR click
   "Scan Provisioned OS Packages (Image)" to list apps embedded in the system image.
2. Review the list of package names, versions, and architectures.
3. Click on any package you want to delete to highlight it.
4. Click "Remove Selected Package" and confirm the prompt.
5. The package will be stripped cleanly without affecting core dependencies.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. TAB 3: AGC SOLID ENGINE (HIGH-RATIO ARCHIVER)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This tab provides native high-compression archiving powered by Windows cabinet.dll.

A. CREATING AN ARCHIVE (.AGC):
   1. Drag and drop files or folders directly into the queue box, or use the 
      "Add Files" / "Add Folder" buttons.
   2. Choose your "Compression Method":
      - Store: Packages files without compression.
      - Fast (MSZIP): Fast compression speed.
      - Ultra (LZMS Solid): Maximum compression dictionary ratio.
   3. Check "Solid archive" for unified solid-block compression.
   4. Check "Test archive" to run an automated integrity verification check.
   5. (Optional) Check "Priority: Low (Bg)" if you are working on large multi-GB
      folders and want your PC to stay fast and responsive in the background.
   6. Click "COMPRESS (.AGC)" and choose where to save the archive.

B. EXTRACTING AN ARCHIVE (.AGC):
   1. Click "Output Dir..." to set where extracted files should go (defaults to Desktop).
   2. Click "EXTRACT (.AGC)".
   3. Select your .agc file. The files and directory structures will unpack
      automatically with real-time progress shown on the bars.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. TROUBLESHOOTING & TIPS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- "Access Denied" or DISM errors: Ensure the program was launched as Administrator.
- Locked Mount Directory: If "WimMount" cannot be deleted manually, go to Tab 1 
  and click "Force DISM Cleanup / Reset".
- Conversion Disk Space: Converting an .esd to .wim requires free temporary disk 
  space equal to the uncompressed size of the image.

